## rule.require.dependency-injection

pass dependencies in, never hardcode them: a procedure says "give me what i need" via the paved `(input, context)` contract
```ts
export const upsert = async (
  { cost }: { cost: JobLeadCost },
  context: { dbConnection: DatabaseConnection; log: LogMethods },
) => {
  context.log.debug('began.upsert', { cost });
  return context.dbConnection.query('SELECT * FROM ...');
};
```
why: testable (inject a fake) · flexible (swap the implementation) · explicit (the wires show) · reusable (the logic runs with any tool). outer layers decide; inner logic behaves
